-- title:
--   Support window for the Iwasawa ratios of a double-coset test function
-- statement:
--   Let $K\subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, let $D$ be an idelic Galois descent datum for $L/K$ (a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to ring automorphisms of the adele ring of $L$, compatible with the inclusion of $L$ and continuous), let $\sigma\in\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal O_K$, and let $\varphi_a$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adele ring of $L$ and a family $\varphi_S$ of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ be given. The assertion is: for every finite set $T$ of primes of $\mathcal O_K$ and every choice $w_v$ of a prime of $\mathcal O_L$ lying over each $v$, there are $A_0\ge 0$ and reals $c_S,c_\infty$ such that for all families $\rho_v\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$, all $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adele ring of $L$ and all $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adele ring, if $(\varphi,\varphi_a,\varphi_f)$ is a semi-local factorisation relative to $S\cup T$ for the local family which at $v\in T$ is the indicator of the double coset $\mathcal K_v\{\rho_v\}\mathcal K_v$ (the semi-local integral set times the semi-local component of the local embedding of $\rho_v$ times the semi-local integral set) and at $v\notin T$ is $\varphi_S(v)$ — that is, $\varphi_a$ is an archimedean test factor, $\varphi_f$ a finite test factor, each member at $v\in S\cup T$ a semi-local test function, $\varphi_f(h)=\prod_{v\in S\cup T}$ of the local factors at the semi-local components of $h$ whenever all components off $S\cup T$ are integral, $\varphi_f(h)=0$ when some component off $S\cup T$ is not integral, and $\varphi(g)=\varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_f)$ — then for every $t\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries, every $b$ in the adelic Borel subgroup, every $k$ in the adelic maximal compact subgroup (finite part integral, each archimedean component a row isometry) and every idele unit $z$ with $\varphi\bigl((bk)^{-1}\,t\,\sigma_D(z\cdot bk)\bigr)\neq 0$, and for $A,B,E$ the $(0,0)$, $(1,1)$ and $(0,1)$ entries of $b^{-1}t\,\sigma_D(z\cdot b)$, one has: $\|B_w/A_w\|=1$ and $\|E_w/A_w\|\le 1$ for all $w\mid v$ with $v\notin S\cup T$; $|\log\|B_w/A_w\||\le A_0(1+\log\mu_v)$ and $\log^+\|E_w/A_w\|\le A_0(1+\log\mu_v)$ for $w\mid v$ with $v\in T$, where $\mu_v$ is the semi-local Haar measure of that double coset at $v$; the same two quantities are $\le c_S$ for $w\mid v$ with $v\in S\setminus T$; and $|\log\|B_w/A_w\||\le c_\infty$, $\log^+\|E_w/A_w\|\le c_\infty$ at every infinite place $w$ of $L$.
--
--   This is the pointwise, place-by-place support window in Iwasawa coordinates for a twisted Hecke double-coset test function: it records that only the ratios $B/A$ and $E/A$ of the diagonal and unipotent entries are constrained, with the constants chosen uniformly in the Hecke datum and in $b$, $k$, $z$ and $t$, and with the bound at the primes of $T$ growing only logarithmically in the Haar volume of the double coset. It feeds the logarithmic height excursion bound for the twisted orbital data and the corresponding window statement for the orbital integral of the double coset.
